==Battleground==
*4 [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 70~73.33 seconds<sup>2,100f~2,200f</sup>.
*2 [[Zomboe]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Sunfish Jones]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[M. Ost]] spawns.
**1 [[Professor A.]] spawns.
**1 [[Croakley]] spawns.
**2 [[Zomboe]]s spawn, delay 53.33~56.67 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
You are able to stall for max wallet at the start of the stage, which you can also use to stack [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunks]] if you wish to. Doing so makes the stage significantly easier as it holds off the pushing power of M. Ost for a while until Croakley eventually catches up to the stack. For attackers, [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapsticks]] and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife]] provide consistent damage output, and [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Mina]] can be useful to Weaken the M. Ost and deal damage to the Professor A. in the back. [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling]] can also occasionally land hits on the Zomboes that spawn during the boss wave or even M. Ost if provided an opportunity with the [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt Cannon|Thunderbolt Cannon]]. Similarly, should you have [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]] at this point, she can deal a great amount of damage to M. Ost if timed correctly and/or assisted by Thunderbolt.

On higher difficulties, it's highly recommended to use units such as [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Uril]], [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Luza]], [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Doron]], and Idi to deal with M. Ost quickly before the stage gets out of hand.

Ubers with high range such as [[Sea Serpent Daliasan (Uber Rare Cat)|Daliasan]] and [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Cosmo]] can make the stage easier by providing consistent damage to the backline.

==Trivia==
*Every single enemy here has the [[Slow|slow]] ability.
*The Belated Priest's name may hint at how all of the stage's enemies can slow cats, as slowness leads to belatedness.
*Prior to [[Version 11.5 Update|Version 11.5]], [[Zomboe]] spawned infinitely after hitting the base, rather than only twice.

